IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `comp50-nouns`
IMPORT `comp50-cross-references`

-- Row il-50. EXPECTED RED: eight assertions, all failing, two about each of the four defects. The count (8) is declared in check.sh and in encoding.json.
-- Each states what the citing words need.
-- Defect 1: regulation 8 of the Fees Regulations prints a Hebrew date and a Gregorian date that name days 29 days apart, so the pair does not agree and a day between them is answered by neither half alone.
-- Defect 2: regulation 66 of the Compromise Regulations prints a Hebrew date and a Gregorian date 366 days apart, with the same two consequences.
-- Defect 4: five signature lines of Kovetz HaTakanot 7639 print a Hebrew date and a Gregorian date 3 days apart, so the pair does not agree, in the first line or in all five.
-- Defect 3: section 367(א)(1) of the Companies Law keeps Ordinance section numbers that section 359 items (4) and (5) of the later law cancel. The first assertion rests on the page images alone;
-- the second rests on the Ordinance consolidation's placing of chapters 11 to 17 and is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY. Nothing here is edited to make it pass.

§ `Defect 1: the commencement pair of the Fees Regulations`

-- 1. The Hebrew half and the Gregorian half name the same day.
#ASSERT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`)
-- 2. A day in the middle of the span between the two halves is answered by the text: the regulations are in force on 15 January 2001.
#ASSERT `the regulations are in force on` (`date pair: Fees Regulations, regulation 8, the commencement day`) (Date 15 1 2001) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Defect 2: the last-day pair of the Compromise Regulations`

-- 3. The Hebrew half and the Gregorian half name the same day.
#ASSERT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`)
-- 4. A day in the middle of the span between the two halves is answered by the text: the temporary provision is in force on 1 January 2008.
#ASSERT `the temporary provision is in force on` (`date pair: Compromise Regulations, regulation 66, the last day of the temporary provision`) (Date 1 1 2008) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Defect 3: the saving clause of the Companies Law`

-- 5. The first range of the clause (Ordinance sections 164 to 201) shares no number with the sections 195 to 201 that the later law cancels (page images).
#ASSERT `how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 164 to 201`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance ss 195 to 201`) EQUALS 0
-- 6. The second and third ranges of the clause (244 to 367 and 370 to 382) share no number with the chapters 11 to 17 that the later law cancels, as the Ordinance consolidation places them (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY).
#ASSERT (`how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 244 to 367`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`)) PLUS (`how many numbers two runs share` (`the clause keeps: Ordinance ss 370 to 382`) (`the later law cancels: Ordinance chapters 11 to 17, as ss 244 to 382`)) EQUALS 0

§ `Defect 4: the five signature lines of one issue`

-- 7. The Hebrew half and the Gregorian half of the first signature line name the same day.
#ASSERT `the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`)
-- 8. The Hebrew half and the Gregorian half agree in all five signature lines.
#ASSERT (`the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 1 of 5, p. 946, the regulations relieving the duty to set a compensation policy`)) AND (`the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 2 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on notice of a general meeting`)) AND (`the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 3 of 5, p. 948, the regulations on how long a resolution is valid`)) AND (`the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 4 of 5, p. 949, the regulations on outside directors who are not Israeli residents`)) AND (`the printed pair agrees` (`date pair: KT 7639 signature line 5 of 5, p. 949, the order changing the First Schedule A to the Law`))
